# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
# Output commands from the unmodified Kick host, checked against the control surface firmware's LED table.
#
#   cmake -S Firmware/kick-mcu -B build/mcu -G Ninja && cmake --build build/mcu
#   emu/run.sh --firmware --script emu/tests/firmware-leds.script
#
# kick-mcu-sim plays the MCU and `expect led` / `expect pad` read its table. What the host sends
# on its own is small: at startup it clears every pad (PAD_SET_ALL_SINGLE_COLOUR, Trans). It sends
# button LEDs only from events the emulator does not produce (transport, bank changes from a
# loaded project), so the button, blink and strip paths are covered by the replay trace
# (emu/tests/traces/leds.trace) and the unit tests, not by this script.
expect streaming
wait 3000
expect pad 1 off 3000
expect pad 8 off 3000
expect pad 16 off 3000
